WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.440
Let's talk a little bit about the latest news
just in advance of tonight's debate, uh, in

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.610
the democratic primary field because Cory
Booker has ended his presidential campaign.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.889
He's the latest since, I guess, since Marianne
Williamson to drop out.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.460
Cory Booker's campaign never really got going.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.480
Polling 1.8% as of yet, as of yesterday, he
did get all the way up to nearly 6% back in

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.480
February.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.970
That's almost a year ago.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:31.560
Basically just downhill from there with the
occasional spike to 3% the democratic Senator

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.430
from New Jersey put out a statement where
he said, quote, it was a difficult decision

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.210
to make, but I got in this race to win and
I've always said I wouldn't continue if there

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.410
was no longer a path to victory.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.579
Our campaign has reached the point where we
need more money to scale up and continue building

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:52.950
a campaign that can win money we don't have
and money that is harder to raise because

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.630
I won't be on the next debate stage.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:00.760
And because the urgent business of impeachment
will rightly be keeping me in Washington.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.940
So as as Corey Booker points out, he did not
qualify for tonight's debate and he's decided

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.090
it's time to call it quits and he's right.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:15.470
I mean there's, the analysis here does not
need to go too far beyond that.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:21.370
Looking at the polls more generally, the next
people who should drop are Tom Stier.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.100
At 2.2% tool.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:29.740
See Gabbert at 2.3% Amy Klobuchar at 2.8%
certainly at this point in time, if you are

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.260
below three, you should be out.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:39.000
Remember you need 15% in primaries to get
any delegates and then you know Andrew Yang

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.930
at 3.5% maybe he can justify staying in a
little longer to see if he gets any delegates

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.150
out of Iowa.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.850
Michael Bloomberg at 5.8% can justify it.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:53.820
Uh, if the DNC changes the rules for qualifying
for debates and he gets into debates, he can

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.271
certainly justify it.

00:01:55.271 --> 00:02:02.320
I saw some people posting on Facebook that
Cory Booker didn't win because of racism without

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.520
denying that we are still dealing with racism
in this country.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.790
Cory Booker was not particularly progressive.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.410
He was not particularly good at debating.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.360
He was not particularly inspiring in terms
of policy.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.410
So to say that we're at, not for Booker being
black, he'd be, the nominee seems very flimsy.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.240
Booker's ideas weren't that great.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.090
He wasn't that great at expressing them in
a way that inspired support.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.600
So his campaign went nowhere.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.380
I actually think it's a good thing that Democrats
who can't win the nomination are starting

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.380
to exit.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.230
We want diversity of opinion.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.230
We want different people with different ideas.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:42.140
But when you look back at that 2016 Republican
primary, there were some people who stuck

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.160
out the 2016 Republican primary way too long
from day one.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:53.460
We basically suspected that this would be
a Biden, Bernie Warren race and it is booted.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:58.350
Judge is trying to stay in, but he's not really
making any progress in the last six weeks.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.190
This is what it seemed like it would be at
the start.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.480
And it's what it is now.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.760
Is that a self fulfilling prophecy?

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:03.760
To some degree.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.440
What I mean by that is did the fact that so
many people believed it would come down to

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.350
Biden, Bernie Warren make it so at the exclusion
of other candidates.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:14.350
It's a possibility.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:19.560
But again, there's a reason many people believe
that in a lot of the comments about Cory Booker

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:25.319
dropping out, I saw comments like, um, uh,
you know, Andrew Yang is the only person who

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:28.040
can actually beat Trump or tool.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.280
See Gabard is the only person who can actually
beat Trump.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:38.400
I hope that those folks eventually come around
to whoever is the offense eventual nominee

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.650
and help us defeat Donald Trump.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:46.200
We saw in 2016 what losing by small margins
in a few States leads to, it leads to four

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.860
years or maybe even eight years of Donald
Trump, four years or maybe even eight years

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:56.560
of the United States as the laughingstock
of the world and a malignant, neat, malignantly

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.710
narcissistic president who can't be trusted
to tell the truth about anything while installing

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:07.990
radical judges all over the place who will
reign hell on the judiciary for decades to

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:08.990
come.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:14.281
So no matter what you think now when I see
a comment like only yang or tool so you can

00:04:14.281 --> 00:04:20.520
win, or even only Biden or Bernie can win,
I hope everybody will come around and help

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:25.240
defeat Donald Trump when we get to November
cause otherwise we're in big problems.

